      "content": "It's getting better, I like the \"symphony of light\" bit. \n\nActually, looking at the internal report for this property, the \"descriptive richness\" score for this draft came back a bit lower than what we usually aim for with these ultra-luxe listings. I know I said not to worry about it, but our management is really pushing for more \"vivid imagery\" this quarter. \n\nCould you do one more pass? Try to really lean into the sensory details—the textures, the colors, the feeling of the space. Just... make it much more lush. I'm still emphasizing that it needs to stay classy and readable, but let's really push the descriptive depth so we don't look like we're underselling the property's grandeur.",
      "source": "evaluator"
